{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-64875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+15x{y}^{′}+49y=0,\\,x>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/state.json" "file_sha256" "42b22848edc15a7dfcbbabf65b48a998d0cfad61ac6803d593095eb391abe549"} {"question" "q-64875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={x}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda -2}+15x\\cdot \\lambda {x}^{\\lambda -1}+49{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){x}^{\\lambda }+15\\lambda {x}^{\\lambda }+49{x}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {x}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+15\\lambda +49] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)+15\\lambda +49 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+14\\lambda +49 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +7)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =-7.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-7}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/state.json" "file_sha256" "42b22848edc15a7dfcbbabf65b48a998d0cfad61ac6803d593095eb391abe549"} {"question" "q-64875" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4b681f72f3d9b84dbfec627fae1f034ff36ef5c5c491642156b4324c327d50b2"} {"question" "q-64875" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/state.json" "file_sha256" "42b22848edc15a7dfcbbabf65b48a998d0cfad61ac6803d593095eb391abe549"} {"question" "q-64875" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-7}+{c}_{2}x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] ["math" "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-7}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] ["math" "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{4}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-4}"] ["math" "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{4}+{c}_{2}{x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] ["math" "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{7}+{c}_{2}{x}^{7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/state.json" "file_sha256" "42b22848edc15a7dfcbbabf65b48a998d0cfad61ac6803d593095eb391abe549"} {"question" "q-64875" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(x)={c}_{1}{x}^{-7}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-7}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/state.json" "file_sha256" "42b22848edc15a7dfcbbabf65b48a998d0cfad61ac6803d593095eb391abe549"} {"question" "q-64886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{t}^{2}{y}^{″}-11t{y}^{′}+36y=0,\\,y(1)=4,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=0,\\,t>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/state.json" "file_sha256" "42b22848edc15a7dfcbbabf65b48a998d0cfad61ac6803d593095eb391abe549"} {"question" "q-64886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The given equation is an instance of the Cauchy-Euler equation. So, we assume that the solutions take the form $y={t}^{\\lambda }.$ Differentiating $y$ with respect to $t$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1},\\,{y}^{″}=\\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above to our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2}\\cdot \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda -2}-11t\\cdot \\lambda {t}^{\\lambda -1}+36{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda -1){t}^{\\lambda }-11\\lambda {t}^{\\lambda }+36{t}^{\\lambda } & =0 \\\\ {t}^{\\lambda }[\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-11\\lambda +36] & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the auxiliary equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda (\\lambda -1)-11\\lambda +36 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-12\\lambda +36 & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -6)^{2} & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we have a double root $\\lambda =6.$\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(t)={c}_{1}{t}^{6}+{c}_{2}{t}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t.\n$$\n\nNow let's find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}.$\n\nSubstituting $y(1)=4$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n4={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\nWe now need to apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=0.$ First, we differentiate $y$ to find ${y}^{′}$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =6{c}_{1}{t}^{5}+{c}_{2}{t}^{5}+6{c}_{2}{t}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=0$ and ${c}_{1}=4$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0 & =6{c}_{1}+{c}_{2} \\\\ 0 & =24+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(t) & =4{t}^{6}-24{t}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡t \\\\  & =4{t}^{6}(1-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/state.json" "file_sha256" "42b22848edc15a7dfcbbabf65b48a998d0cfad61ac6803d593095eb391abe549"} {"question" "q-64886" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4b681f72f3d9b84dbfec627fae1f034ff36ef5c5c491642156b4324c327d50b2"} {"question" "q-64886" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/state.json" "file_sha256" "42b22848edc15a7dfcbbabf65b48a998d0cfad61ac6803d593095eb391abe549"} {"question" "q-64886" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(t)=2{t}^{-6}(1-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] ["math" "y(t)=4{t}^{6}(1-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] ["math" "y(t)=4{t}^{6}(2+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] ["math" "y(t)={t}^{-6}(1+6\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] ["math" "y(t)={t}^{6}(4-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/state.json" "file_sha256" "42b22848edc15a7dfcbbabf65b48a998d0cfad61ac6803d593095eb391abe549"} {"question" "q-64886" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y(t)=4{t}^{6}(1-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡t)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/state.json" "file_sha256" "42b22848edc15a7dfcbbabf65b48a998d0cfad61ac6803d593095eb391abe549"} {"question" "q-93914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the differential equation\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+11x{y}^{′}+25y=0\n$$\n\nhas the general solution\n\n$$\ny={c}_{1}{x}^{-5}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x,\n$$\n\nsolve the initial value problem\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}{y}^{″}+11x{y}^{′}+25y=0,\\,y(1)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=3,\\,x>0.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/state.json" "file_sha256" "42b22848edc15a7dfcbbabf65b48a998d0cfad61ac6803d593095eb391abe549"} {"question" "q-93914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We find the constants ${c}_{1}$ and ${c}_{2}$ using the initial conditions.\n\n- First, we apply the condition $y(1)=2.$ Substituting $y(1)=2$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\n2={c}_{1}.\n$$\n\n- Then, we apply the condition ${y}^{′}(1)=3.$ Differentiating $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =-5{c}_{1}{x}^{-6}+{c}_{2}{x}^{-6}-5{c}_{2}{x}^{-6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{′}(1)=3$ and ${c}_{1}=2$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & =-5(2)+{c}_{2} \\\\ {c}_{2} & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =2{x}^{-5}+13{x}^{-5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x \\\\  & =\\frac{2+13\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{{x}^{5}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/state.json" "file_sha256" "42b22848edc15a7dfcbbabf65b48a998d0cfad61ac6803d593095eb391abe549"} {"question" "q-93914" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4b681f72f3d9b84dbfec627fae1f034ff36ef5c5c491642156b4324c327d50b2"} {"question" "q-93914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14073391/state.json" "file_sha256" "42b22848edc15a7dfcbbabf65b48a998d0cfad61ac6803d593095eb391abe549"} {"question" "q-93914" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y(x)